 "round": 1, "verdict": "unclear"}, "owner": {"at": "2026-10-25T07:49:50+00:00", "decision": "D69", "reason": "owner 2026-10-25 (D69): write the researcher''s value with its found quote for a cell the re-check held as unclear"}}]'::jsonb),
    ('3962491a-58ec-4e7c-a1be-3c456f9818a6'::uuid, 'period_name', '4500 - 3000 BC', '3000 - 1500 BC', 'fields-wd5-2026-10-25p-s003:3962491a-58ec-4e7c-a1be-3c456f9818a6:period_name', 'fields-wd5-2026-10-25p-s003 (wd5-derive-period-name): period_start -1600 (written in this step)', '[{"source": "pipeline/utils/text.py:categorize_period", "url": "pipeline/utils/text.py", "quote": "categorize_period(-1600) = ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "output/remediation/gold_standard/GOLD_STANDARD.md:79", "url": "output/remediation/gold_standard/GOLD_STANDARD.md", "quote": "| `period_name` | equals `categorize_period(period_start)` |"}, {"source": "WD5 decision (counted, round 0, field_researcher:wd5-r0-b0038)", "decision": "replace", "status": "MISSING", "reasoning": "The Minchinhampton Local History Group reports Timothy Darvill''s view (Prehistoric Gloucestershire) that the Longstone and the neighbouring standing stones date from the Bronze Age, 1600 to 700 BC, and Wikipedia''s Minchinhampton article likewise says the Longstone more probably dates to the Bronze Age; the same page also mentions a Neolithic long-barrow theory (3500 to 2500 BC) that Darvill thinks unlikely, so the hedged Bronze Age start of 1600 BC is taken.", "value_page": null, "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5 (Claude Code agent)", "adversarial": {"answered_by": "adversarial:adv-r1-b0003", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5 (Claude Code agent)", "reason": "The sources disagree and nothing excavated dates the stone: the local history group offers a Neolithic long-barrow stone (3500-2500 BC) against Darvill''s Bronze Age group (1600-700 BC), Stone Bothering says over four millennia old, and Historic England gives only the class range Late Neolithic to Bronze Age. -1600 is one hypothesis, not a dated start.", "round": 1, "verdict": "unclear"}, "owner": {"at": "2026-10-25T07:49:50+00:00", "decision": "D69", "reason": "owner 2026-10-25 (D69): write the researcher''s value with its found quote for a cell the 